{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-008", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Sodium-ion batteries approach cost parity with LFP, with 70 GWh covered by supply agreements", "content": "<p>Sodium-ion batteries are approaching cell-level cost parity with LFP technology, with supply agreements exceeding 70 GWh worldwide. Despite higher upfront costs, they could offer a 21% lower total cost of ownership over 20 years, according to Wood Mackenzie.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/sodium-ion-batteries-approach-cost-parity-with-lfp-with-70-gwh-covered-by-supply-agreements/\">Sodium-ion batteries approach cost parity with LFP, with 70 GWh covered by suppl", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/sodium-ion-batteries-approach-cost-parity-with-lfp-with-70-gwh-covered-by-supply-agreements/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-009", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: H2 turbines can push LCOHS to around $0.62/kg", "content": "<p>Australian researchers found that hydrogen gas turbines could provide more cost-effective backup power than fuel cells during periods of low solar availability. Their study highlights how reservoir properties and system design affect the cost and performance of underground hydrogen storage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/the-hydrogen-stream-h2-turbines-can-push-lcohs-to-around-0-62-kg/\">The Hydrogen Stream: H2 turbines can push LCOHS to around $0.62/kg</a> app", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/the-hydrogen-stream-h2-turbines-can-push-lcohs-to-around-0-62-kg/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "longi-2026-11-06-010", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["longi", "tongwei"], "customers": ["longi"], "suppliers": ["tongwei"]}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.85, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Chinese PV Industry Brief: JA, Longi, Tongwei report widening losses", "content": "<p>JA, Longi and Tongwei reported widening net losses for the first nine months of 2026, as revenue fell 23.62%, 13.85% and 9.69% year on year, respectively.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/chinese-pv-industry-brief-ja-longi-tongwei-report-widening-losses/\">Chinese PV Industry Brief: JA, Longi, Tongwei report widening losses</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/chinese-pv-industry-brief-ja-longi-tongwei-report-widening-losses/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-011", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Soluxtec resumes TOPCon solar module production in Germany", "content": "<p>The German solar module manufacturer has restarted production at its Trier-Föhren facility after upgrading its manufacturing lines to produce G12-format TOPCon modules. The company has yet to disclose the annual production capacity of the modernized plant.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/soluxtec-resumes-topcon-solar-module-production-in-germany/\">Soluxtec resumes TOPCon solar module production in Germany</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.c", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/soluxtec-resumes-topcon-solar-module-production-in-germany/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-012", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "World’s largest liquid-air storage facility comes online in China", "content": "<p>China’s 60 MW/600 MWh liquid-air energy storage facility in Qinghai began generating electricity on October 30, marking a major milestone in long-duration energy storage commercialization. The world’s largest grid-connected LAES project offers 10 hours of continuous power output, supporting renewable energy integration with domestically developed technology.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/worlds-largest-liquid-air-storage-facility-comes-online-in-china/\">World", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/worlds-largest-liquid-air-storage-facility-comes-online-in-china/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-013", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "S-5! presents height-adjustable mounting system for PV modules on metal roofs", "content": "<p>S-5! has introduced the PVKIT 3.0, a rail-less mounting system for solar panels on metal roofs, available with an optional 50 mm clearance for wiring and power electronics. The system features non-penetrating attachments and accommodates PV module frames ranging from 25 mm to 35 mm, depending on the configuration.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/s-5-presents-height-adjustable-mounting-system-for-pv-modules-on-metal-roofs/\">S-5! presents height-adjustable mounti", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/s-5-presents-height-adjustable-mounting-system-for-pv-modules-on-metal-roofs/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-014", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "October 2026 good for PV Production in Europe, but South of France and Ukraine missout", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for pv magazine, <b>Solcast</b>, a DNV company, reports that solar irradiance across much of Europe was around 10% above average in October 2026, reaching up to 25% above average in central Europe and the Baltic States due to persistent high-pressure systems.<br />\nHowever, southern France and the Black Sea region experienced below-average irradiance due to cloud cover and storms, while severe winds caused widespread power outages across western Europe.</p>\n<p>The post ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/october-2026-good-for-pv-production-in-europe-but-south-of-france-and-ukraine-missout/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-015", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Türkiye targets 175 GW of solar, wind capacity by 2040", "content": "<p>Türkiye's energy vision for 2040 aims to increase renewables' share of the country's total installed capacity to 77%, from around 63% today.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/turkiye-targets-175-gw-of-solar-wind-capacity-by-2040/\">Türkiye targets 175 GW of solar, wind capacity by 2040</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/turkiye-targets-175-gw-of-solar-wind-capacity-by-2040/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-016", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "U.S. startup secures $9 million to scale production of 22.33%-efficient perovskite solar modules", "content": "<p>U.S.-based RadianX has secured $9 million in financing to scale production of perovskite solar modules for connected devices and IoT applications. The company plans to establish an automated 6 MW production line.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/u-s-startup-secures-9-million-to-scale-production-of-22-33-efficient-perovskite-solar-modules/\">U.S. startup secures $9 million to scale production of 22.33%-efficient perovskite solar modules</a> appeared first on <a hr", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/u-s-startup-secures-9-million-to-scale-production-of-22-33-efficient-perovskite-solar-modules/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "longi-2026-11-06-017", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["longi"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Longi achieves 35.31% efficiency in perovskite-silicon tandem solar cell based on self-assembled molecules", "content": "<p>Longi has developed a perovskite-silicon tandem solar cell with a certified efficiency of 35.25% by using specially engineered molecules to improve interface quality and charge extraction. The device also demonstrated enhanced operational stability, retaining 94% of its initial efficiency after 1,500 hours of continuous operation.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/longi-achieves-35-31-efficiency-in-perovskite-silicon-tandem-solar-cell-based-on-self-assembled-mole", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/06/longi-achieves-35-31-efficiency-in-perovskite-silicon-tandem-solar-cell-based-on-self-assembled-molecules/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-018", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "“Moving into a positive political environment for solar” – is the ITC coming back?", "content": "Starting immediately after the signing of the OBBB, there has been speculation that the solar tax credit would come back, including nine pieces of legislation filed by U.S. Senators and Representatives.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/11/06/moving-into-a-positive-political-environment-for-solar-is-the-itc-coming-back/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-06-019", "date": "2026-11-06", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "U.S. solar developers navigate policy stack as Section 232 deadline nears", "content": "With national inventory surging 126% in the second quarter of 2026 ahead of shifting trade cutoffs, utility-scale developers are altering procurement strategies and contracts to manage multi-layered regulatory uncertainty.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine_usa", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/11/06/u-s-solar-developers-navigate-policy-stack-as-section-232-deadline-nears/", "type": "rss"}]}
